--- !u!114 &7292266245737022391
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>1.</b>  Make sure the <b>Ball</b> GameObject is still selected.
      \n\n<b>2.</b>  In the <b>Inspector</b> window, in the <b>Transform</b> component,
      set the <b>Ball</b> GameObject's <b>Scale</b> to <b>X = 0.25, Y = 0.25,</b>
      and <b>Z = 0.25.</b>\n\n<b>Note: </b> You can also select the chain link icon
      next to the <b>Scale</b> properties to enable or disable <b>constrained proportions.</b>
      When this is enabled, changing one scale property automatically changes the
      other two by the same amount. "
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &7348288420726687660
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You'll now fix the ramp by adding a collider component, which
      is essential for physical interactions in Unity. A collider is a component
      that defines the shape of an object for the purpose of physical collisions
      and interactions within the environment. Without a collider, an object has
      no physical boundaries and other objects can go right through it \u2014 like
      a cloud.\n\nThe sphere primitive you added earlier for the ball already came
      with a <b>Sphere</b> collider \u2014 that's what the Physics Material is attached
      to.\n\nUnity provides various collider shapes (such as sphere, cube, and capsule
      colliders). However, since the ramp has an irregular shape, you\u2019ll use
      something called a <b>Mesh</b> collider, which conforms to the unique shape
      of the object\u2019s mesh (3D shape)."
--- !u!114 &7681780521032908999
